tags: [parse, syntax, naming-convention, pascal-case, type, record]
description: "Type or variant name must be formatted in PascalCase"
---

Type and variant names in Kura must use `PascalCase`, starting with an uppercase letter (`A–Z`) with no hyphens (such as `Point`, `UserProfile`, or `ClickEvent`). Lowercase or `kebab-case` type names are not permitted.

## Example

This error occurs when a `type` declaration or variant constructor begins with a lowercase letter or contains hyphens:

```kura
type user-profile = {
  name: String,
  age: Int,
}

type status = active | inactive
```

## Solution

Capitalize the type and variant names using `PascalCase`:

```kura
type UserProfile = {
  name: String,
  age: Int,
}

type Status = Active | Inactive
```
